cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SiCoPR-Assist"
message: >-
  If you refer to this software, please cite it using the metadata below. It is
  a front end that drives SiCoPR; every COM result it reports comes from SiCoPR,
  so cite SiCoPR as well when the results are the subject.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bermensolo
    given-names: Todd
repository-code: "https://github.com/tbermen/SiCoPR-Assist"
version: "0.13.0"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
abstract: >-
  A rules-based front end for SiCoPR, the Python port of the IEEE 802.3 Channel
  Operating Margin (COM) Reference Code. It turns a typed phrase (a re-run with
  a changed parameter, a sweep, a crosstalk case, a channel download from the
  IEEE P802.3dj tools page) into one of three outcomes, a plan, a question or a
  refusal with its reason, validates every change against a parameter schema
  and the engine's own loader, carries the plan out through SiCoPR, and keeps
  a history of every run. It runs from the command line or as a panel in
  SiCoPR's GUI.
keywords:
  - channel operating margin
  - COM
  - IEEE 802.3
  - signal integrity
  - SerDes
license: BSD-3-Clause
references:
  - type: software
    title: "SiCoPR"
    authors:
      - family-names: Bermensolo
        given-names: Todd
    repository-code: "https://github.com/tbermen/SiCoPR"
    license: BSD-3-Clause
    notes: >-
      The COM engine SiCoPR-Assist drives: a Python port of the IEEE 802.3
      COM MATLAB Reference Code.
